      "message": "Just meat-puppetting, but these seem like real issues.\n\n1. 🔴 Critical: fOrigin / fCreationMatrix Translation Offset Bypasses ValidDirectPosition\nLocation\nsrc/text/gpu/VertexFiller.cpp (VertexFiller::CanUseDirect, VertexFiller::boundsAndDeviceMatrix)\n\nsrc/text/gpu/SlugImpl.cpp (valid_slug_matrices)\n\nAnalysis\nValidDirectPosition bounds leftTop glyph coordinates to [-2^23, 2^23] (kMaxDirectCoord) and checks pt.isFinite() because in Skia, SkScalarIsInt(x) is implemented as x \u003d\u003d sk_float_floor(x):\nEvery float with magnitude ≥ 2²⁴ is an exact integer (SkScalarIsInt(1e25f) \u003d\u003d true).\n\nSkScalarIsInt(SK_ScalarInfinity) evaluates to true because floorf(INFINITY) \u003d\u003d INFINITY.\n\nHowever, SlugImpl::MakeFromBuffer only checks origin.isFinite(), and SubRunContainer::MakeFromBufferInAlloc only checks positionMatrix.isFinite(). At draw time, the actual device-space position of a direct-mask glyph is leftTop[i] + offset, where offset is computed from fOrigin and fCreationMatrix:\nInfinity Bypass: If a crafted Slug sets fOrigin \u003d {2e38f, 0.0f} and fInitialPositionMatrix \u003d fCreationMatrix \u003d SkMatrix::Translate(-2e38f, 0.0f), both pass .isFinite() during deserialization. When drawn with an identity CTM (localToDevice \u003d SkMatrix::I()), offset.fX \u003d 2e38f - (-2e38f) overflows to +Infinity. Because SkScalarIsInt(+Infinity) is true, both CanUseDirect and boundsAndDeviceMatrix accept the draw and produce a non-finite translation matrix / vertex position.\n\nMagnitude \u0026 Precision Bypass: If a crafted Slug sets fOrigin \u003d {1e25f, 0.0f} and fCreationMatrix \u003d SkMatrix::I() with leftTop \u003d {{10.0f, 20.0f}}, deserialization succeeds. At draw time, offset.fX \u003d 1e25f passes SkScalarIsInt(offset.fX) and shifts the drawn vertices to 1e25f, defeating the 2^23 bound enforced by ValidDirectPosition. Furthermore, if fOrigin \u003d {8388608.0f, 0.0f} (2²³) and fCreationMatrix \u003d SkMatrix::Translate(8388608.0f, 0.0f), a fractional canvas translation of 0.5f (localToDevice \u003d SkMatrix::Translate(0.5f, 0.0f)) is absorbed by float rounding (8388608.0f + 0.5f \u003d\u003d 8388608.0f), resulting in offset.fX \u003d 0.0f and allowing the draw instead of dropping it.\n\nSuggestion\nValidate translation / offset with VertexFiller::ValidDirectPosition in CanUseDirect, boundsAndDeviceMatrix, and valid_slug_matrices (or also bound fCreationMatrix translation / fOrigin for direct subruns):\n\n cpp\n\n // In VertexFiller::CanUseDirect (src/text/gpu/VertexFiller.cpp):\nSkVector translation \u003d positionMatrix.mapOrigin() - creationMatrix.mapOrigin();\nreturn {creationMatrix.getScaleX() \u003d\u003d positionMatrix.getScaleX() \u0026\u0026\n        creationMatrix.getScaleY() \u003d\u003d positionMatrix.getScaleY() \u0026\u0026\n        creationMatrix.getSkewX()  \u003d\u003d positionMatrix.getSkewX()  \u0026\u0026\n        creationMatrix.getSkewY()  \u003d\u003d positionMatrix.getSkewY()  \u0026\u0026\n        !positionMatrix.hasPerspective() \u0026\u0026 !creationMatrix.hasPerspective() \u0026\u0026\n        ValidDirectPosition(translation),\n        translation};\n\n// In VertexFiller::boundsAndDeviceMatrix (src/text/gpu/VertexFiller.cpp):\nif (compatibleMatrix) {\n    SkPoint mappedOrigin \u003d localToDevice.mapPoint(drawOrigin);\n    auto offset \u003d mappedOrigin -\n                  SkPoint{fCreationMatrix.getTranslateX(), fCreationMatrix.getTranslateY()};\n    if (ValidDirectPosition(offset)) {\n        return {fCreationBounds, SkMatrix::Translate(offset)};\n    }\n}\n\n2. 🟠 High: Incomplete Bounds Finiteness Validation in prepare_for_* and reconstruct_safe_bounds\nLocation\nsrc/text/gpu/SubRunContainer.cpp (prepare_for_SDFT_drawing, prepare_for_mask_drawing, make_vertex_filler_from_buffer)\n\nAnalysis\nIn prepare_for_SDFT_drawing and prepare_for_mask_drawing:\nThe patch checks:\n\n cpp\n\n const SkGlyphRect glyphBounds \u003d\n        glyph_bounds(digest, SDFTSubRun::kGlyphInsetting, mappedPos);\nif (!glyphBounds.leftTop().isFinite()) {\n    break;\n}\n\n A glyph\u0027s digest.bounds() commonly has negative left/top (e.g., ascenders above the baseline) and positive right/bottom. If mappedPos is positive and close to FLT_MAX (e.g., 3.4028234e38f), glyphBounds.leftTop() (mappedPos + negative_offset) remains finite, whereas glyphBounds.rightBottom() (mappedPos + positive_offset) overflows to +Infinity. This pollutes boundingRect \u003d skglyph::rect_union(boundingRect, glyphBounds) with +Infinity.\n\nIn make_vertex_filler_from_buffer:\nFor non-direct subruns (TransformedMaskSubRun and SDFTSubRun), make_points_from_buffer only checks positionsData[i].isFinite(). If a serialized buffer contains leftTop[i] \u003d {FLT_MAX, FLT_MAX}, reconstruct_safe_bounds adds the glyph\u0027s dimensions to leftTop[i], overflowing safeBounds (fCreationBounds) to +Infinity without validation.\n\nSuggestion\nCheck both leftTop() and rightBottom() (or glyphBounds.rect().isFinite()) in prepare_for_SDFT_drawing and prepare_for_mask_drawing, and validate safeBounds.isFinite() in make_vertex_filler_from_buffer:\n\n cpp\n\n // In prepare_for_SDFT_drawing and prepare_for_mask_drawing:\nif (!glyphBounds.leftTop().isFinite() || !glyphBounds.rightBottom().isFinite()) {\n    continue;\n}\n\n// In make_vertex_filler_from_buffer:\nSkRect safeBounds \u003d reconstruct_safe_bounds(leftTop, glyphVector, actionType, inset);\nif (!buffer.validate(safeBounds.isFinite())) {\n    return std::nullopt;\n}",
